    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=-x^3+16x$. Use $P(-4)=0$ and $P(3)=21$ with $P(x)=ax^3+bx$.",
      "worked": "An odd cubic has the form $P(x)=ax^3+bx$, since $P(-x)=-P(x)$.\n\nBy the factor and remainder theorems,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-4)&=0\\\\-64a-4b&=0\\\\b&=-16a\\\\P(3)&=21\\\\27a+3b&=21\\\\27a+3(-16a)&=21\\\\-21a&=21\\\\a&=-1\\\\b&=16.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $P(x)=-x^3+16x$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
